00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:18.130
Sentence enders such as "-pri" and "-chanko" are used at the end of a sentence...

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:21.240
...to bring across a type of character or atmosphere.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.090
What's "atmosphere"?

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:23.500
What is it?

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:27.210
"Atmosphere" is... "Atmosphere" is...

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:29.270
What you roll rice balls in!

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:30.930
Wrong-pri!

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:36.200
If you use "-pri", you can become a pop idol like Mirelle.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.460
Now then, everyone practise it together.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:39.360
And start!

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:42.580
Pri! Pri! Pri!

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:43.690
One more time.

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:44.790
And start!

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:47.870
Pri! Pri! Pri!

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:49.540
I've memorised "-pri"-pri

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:50.850
I've memorised it-pri.

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:52.910
